# MentalPoker

This repository is being migrated from an experimental v1 implementation to
Protocol v2. The current executable and Compose topology are retained only as a
repeatable legacy baseline. They are not suitable for real-money, token, or
high-value play.

The measured stage-1 environment, results, warnings, and legacy limits are
recorded in
[`docs/baseline/Phase-1-Legacy-Baseline.md`](docs/baseline/Phase-1-Legacy-Baseline.md).

## Prerequisites

The canonical build environment is the pinned Ubuntu 24.04 container. For a
native build, install CMake 3.28+, Ninja, Boost.System/Thread, GMP/GMPXX,
jsoncpp, pkg-config, and a C++20 compiler.

Python 3.12 is used for the legacy lobby and integration runner. Rust 1.98.0 is
pinned now so later stages start from a fixed toolchain; stage 1 does not yet
contain Rust code.

## Native baseline build

```sh
cmake --preset dev-debug
cmake --build --preset dev-debug
ctest --preset dev-debug
```

Release and sanitizer variants use the same source target:

```sh
cmake --preset ci-release
cmake --build --preset ci-release
ctest --preset ci-release

cmake --preset asan-ubsan
cmake --build --preset asan-ubsan
ctest --preset asan-ubsan
```

All generated files are written below `out/`.

## Four-node legacy smoke test

Start Docker, then run:

```sh
./test1.sh
```

The runner builds the pinned images, starts the lobby and four players in a
controlled order, requires every player to finish the existing hand flow, and
repeats the run three times. It exits non-zero on timeout, an early container
exit, a missing phase marker, or sanitizer diagnostics.

Useful options:

```sh
./test1.sh --repeat 1 --timeout 180
./test1.sh --preset asan-ubsan --repeat 1
```

Sanitized logs and a machine-readable summary are written under
`artifacts/legacy-smoke/`. Raw private card lines and large legacy crypto values
are not retained.

The old ten-player script is not a phase-1 acceptance gate and remains an
unverified legacy utility.
